<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean crop 70 pct harvested - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean crop 70 pct harvested - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 70 percent of Brazil's expected soybean crop had been harvested by April 10, consultants Safras e Mercado said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The 70 percent compares with 51 percent by April 11, 1996, a historical average over the past five years of 46 percent and a revised average of 52 percent by April 3 this year, it added.</p>
<p>Last week Safras said that 49 percent of the harvest had been collected by April 3.</p>
<p>The harvest was much faster in the week ending April 10 due to better weather conditions, Safras said.</p>
<p>In Rio Grande do Sul, the harvest proceeded at a particularly fast rate over the past two weeks because of the dry weather which has accelerated crop development.</p>
<p>A breakdown of percentage harvested by state follows.</p>
<p> STATE		     10/04/97   03/04/97   11/04/96  5-yr avge</p>
<p> Rio Grande do Sul	 57	    27*	   8	  17</p>
<p> Parana			86	    74	   78	  76</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		 80	    63	   70	  60</p>
<p> Mato Grosso do Sul	80	    60	   72	  63</p>
<p> Goias			 72	    56	   68	  43</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		   98	    92	   95	  85</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		40	    34	   36	  34</p>
<p> Others			30	    18	   19	  18</p>
<p> TOTAL BRAZIL		70	    52*	  51	  46</p>
<p>* revised figure</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
